  "body": "PR #402's fix makes the **column engine** (`Dexel`, which feeds the post gate's verdict) sweep XY arcs on the true circle. Two other places still draw XY arcs as chords **inside** the arc, and they carry the same two-sided error.\n- **Convex corners:** the simulated tool centre comes up to one sagitta closer to the part than the real G2/G3, which produces false cuts.\n- **Concave corners and bull-nose helices:** it stops up to one sagitta short, which hides real cuts. #402's `arc_sweep` tests found a bull-nose helix column the true arc cuts 2.5 mm deep that the field engine misses.\n\n**Where**\n- `field_cut::chords`: the field engine, used for display and the lathe/rotary views.\n- `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan.rs`: the generator-time envelope scan.\n\nNeither feeds the post gate's verdict, so nothing unsafe reaches G-code today. But the displayed stock and the generator-time envelope readings can differ from the posted motion by up to one sagitta in either direction.\n\n**Proposed:** reuse #402's exact arc sweep (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/dexel_arc.rs`) or its closed-form reach window in both places. Then tighten `stock_bull_nose::both_engines_cut_a_bull_nose_alike` back to full engine parity on arcs; #402 relaxed it to `arc_parity`.\n\n**Done means**\n- The field engine and the envelope scan cut XY arcs on the true circle.\n- The engines agree on arcs to the same 1e-5 as on straight moves.\n- A concave and a convex corner case are pinned in each.\n\nFollows #402.\n",
